INFO:root:#TASK III: generate regexr arguments: 

 jython:import re
jython:import re

def clean_name(name):
    return re.sub(r'[^\w\s]', '', name).lower().strip()

unique_dishes = set(map(clean_name, dishes))

dish_count = {}
for dish in unique_dishes:
    dish_count[dish] = 0

for row in dishes:
    cleaned_row = clean_name(row)
    if cleaned_row in dish_count:
        dish_count[cleaned_row] += 1
        if dish_count[cleaned_row] > 20:
            print("%s" % (The dish '{cleaned_row}' appears more than 20 times.))


This expression first defines a function to clean the names of dishes by removing punctuation, converting to lowercase, and removing extra spaces. Then it finds all unique dish names after cleaning and initializes a dictionary to store the count of each dish. Finally, it counts the occurrences of each dish and checks if any dish appears more than 20 times.
